# DBK protocol

Frames: `call` / `ok` / `error` / `event` / `ping` / `pong`. Handshake `session.hello` with shared token before other RPCs.
App (JVM) calls Gateway (Koishi): `bots.list`, `targets.list`, `targets.get`, `message.send`, `message.recall`.
Gateway events: `bot.changed`, `message.created`.
`message.send` returns `OK | PARTIAL | UNKNOWN | FAILED`. RPC `error` is only for transport/params (missing bot, bad token), not for “Discord said 403”.
Identity: `botKey = platform:selfId`. Target `kind` matches core `TargetKind` as declared by each bot (`target.*` features). Bot `status`: `READY` (online) / `CONNECTING` / `UNAVAILABLE`.
v1 out of scope: event resume by `seq`, media probe, buttons, Koishi command plugins for dynamic-bot. OneBot via Koishi `adapter-onebot` is in scope; do not speak OneBot in this repo.
Spec: `docs/protocol.md`.
